  "worked_solution": "To predict the number of years it will take for the car to be worth $$20\\,000,$ we need to substitute $y=20$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =28-x \\\\ 20 & =28-x \\\\ 20+x & =28 \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, it will take approximately $8$ years for the car to be worth $$20\\,000.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=20$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
